    "originalInstructions": "1. Clean two young rabbits and cut into joints\n2. Soak in salt and water for half an hour\n3. Put into a saucepan with a pint of cold water, a bunch of sweet herbs, an onion finely minced, a pinch of mace, half a nutmeg, a pinch of pepper and half a pound of salt pork cut in small thin slices\n4. Cover and stew until tender\n5. Take out the rabbits and set in a dish where they will keep warm\n6. Add to the gravy a cup of cream or milk, two well-beaten eggs stirred in a little at a time, a tablespoonful of butter, and a thickening made of a tablespoonful of flour and a little milk\n7. Boil up once and remove the saucepan from the fire\n8. Squeeze in the juice of a lemon while stirring\n9. Pour over the rabbits",
